<h2>What is <code>filter: drop-shadow()</code> and how is it different?</h2>

<p>This is where most developers get confused. <code>filter: drop-shadow()</code> is a CSS filter function — it composites the element into an offscreen buffer and paints the shadow from the element's <strong>actual visual outline</strong>, not its bounding box.</p>

<p>The practical difference: if you clip an element with <code>clip-path</code>, or use a PNG/SVG with transparent areas, <code>box-shadow</code> still follows the invisible rectangle. <code>drop-shadow()</code> follows the real shape.</p>

